# api/

`api/openapi.yaml` lives here: the authoritative transport contract for this
application's JSON API. It is hand-edited. The Go server bindings under
`internal/platform/httpapi/openapigen/` are generated from it now; the
frontend TypeScript models will use the same source contract when added.

Edit `openapi.yaml`, then run `make api-generate`. The pinned oapi-codegen
tool writes strict chi models and server bindings to
`internal/platform/httpapi/openapigen/openapi.gen.go`. `make api-check`
performs the same generation into a temporary file and fails on a byte
difference without modifying the checked-in output; it is part of `make all`.

Paths in the document are relative to the `/api/v1` server and router
boundary. For example, `/widgets` becomes `/api/v1/widgets`; do not repeat
the version prefix in every OpenAPI path. The initial bodyless API index at
`GET /api/v1/` is only a wiring fixture, not a health endpoint.

The API and document routers are sibling security boundaries with independent
policies. Application middleware may be added only through the documented
`httpapi.MiddlewareSlots`, inside the fixed security, request identity/logging,
recovery, and metrics core. Keep `router_test.go` current if the application
deliberately changes that contract.

Implement generated operations on the application-owned `httpapi.Server` in
`api.go`. Its compile-time `StrictServerInterface` assertion makes a changed
contract fail the build until every operation has an implementation. Never
edit `openapigen/`; it retains oapi-codegen's standard generated-code header
and is replaced as a complete tool-owned output.
